 | correctness-7 | For the lead: not fixed. `execute_background` gets a `ToolAgent`, which has no telemetry handle, so the agent's `trace_attributes` have to travel `Agent` -> `background_tasks::ToolRun` -> `BackgroundToolRun` (`types/agent.rs`, `background_tasks/`, outside this track). Recommended: add `trace_attributes: Vec<(String, AttributeValue)>` to `ToolRun` and `BackgroundToolRun`, filled where the scheduler builds the run from the agent (a new `LocalTracer::trace_attributes()` getter), and call `telemetry.lock().tracer.set_trace_attributes(..)` on the run's `LocalTelemetry` in `tools/executors/executor.rs` before the `ToolTerminal` is built; extend the DIVERGENCES row at `docs/DIVERGENCES.md:79` until then. | - |
 | parity-14 | Fixed (staged row): `Local trace ids` in `.rust-port/staging/p10fixa/divergences.md`, with the rows for the behaviour changes of correctness-1, correctness-3, correctness-6 and parity-5. | this commit |
 | api-11 | Fixed: the two `otel`-only extension-trait imports of `telemetry/tracer/memory.rs` are at the top of the file under `#[cfg(feature = "otel")]`. No behaviour change. | this commit |
+| parity-10 | Fixed for this track's specs: `docs/test-title-map.json` has the entries for `telemetry/json`, `local-trace`, `meter`, `tracer.test.node` and `memory/memory-tracing`; the checker prints `ok` for the last four, and for `json.test.ts` once the staged row (`9/15`, `.rust-port/staging/p10fixa/parity.md`) replaces the PARITY.md row. `config.test.node.ts` (:37, :252, :268) is p10fixb's spec and is left to it. | this commit |
